  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: between Sermonae and Agiria</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An unlocated Roman road station that, according to the Antonine Itinerary, was located between Agiria (modern Calamocha or Salvaca\u00f1ete?) and Sermonae (Cari\u00f1ena?) on the Roman road from Laminium (Alhambra?) to Caesaraugusta (Zaragosa). It may be the same place as one \"Caraca\" mentioned by the Geographer of Ravenna as lying between Complutum (Alcal\u00e1 de Henares) and \"Puteis\".",
  "reprPoint": [
    -1.314129,
    41.087041
  ],
